Static:
    - variables or methods
    - an attribute or method belongs to a Class instead of an instance of a class
    - example: Standard Math Class

Static Method Rules:
    - You cannot call a static method from an instance method
    - You can call a static method from a static method
    - You can call an instance method from a static method
    - You can call an instance method from an instance method

Static methods are used for:
    - Class constants
    - Object Counters

Note: Helper methods are usually static because you don't want to have to create
an instance for the helper method.